# Task-local OHOS signing tool resolution must follow the frozen compiler closure.
id:                     E2174-draft-A7F3
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|binary-sign-tool|llvm-objcopy
phase:                  package|target-validation|w3
error_signature:        '/data/service/hnp/bin/(?:binary-sign-tool|llvm-objcopy): inaccessible or not found|Error 127 while executing.*sign'
severity:               2
category:               ohos|toolchain|signing|task_owned_environment
match_keywords:         OHOS signing tool path, task-owned toolchain, usr/local/bin, binary-sign-tool, llvm-objcopy, Conan package
root_cause:             A recipe assumed signing utilities lived in a system HNP directory, but the target exposed the frozen compiler and signing tools only through the task-visible user-local bin directory. The build and compile phases therefore succeeded while package signing failed with shell status 127.
affected_scope:         OHOS Conan recipes that sign ELF libraries or executables during package() and run on devices where system HNP paths are absent or read-only.
verification_cmd:       Resolve each tool from compiler conf, PATH, compiler directory, task home usr/local/bin, and system fallback; require executable files before package(); verify the emitted command path and signed output in the target log.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           frozen-closure-tool-resolution
rec_description:        Resolve signing tools from the task's compiler configuration and environment before consulting system paths. Fail closed when either required tool is absent, and never copy a tool into a shared system directory. Bind the resolver and tool paths to the candidate recipe hash and verify the final package log.
rec_command:            'resolve llvm-objcopy and binary-sign-tool from conf/PATH/compiler-dir/task-home/system; fail if missing; sign package ELF outputs'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      task_owned_tool_bootstrap
fallback_description:   If the device lacks the required tools, transfer a frozen, hash-bound executable closure into the task-owned root/bin and validate bytes, mode, and version before prepare. Do not modify /data/service/hnp or other shared directories.
fallback_command:       'transfer exact tool closure to task-owned bin; read back SHA-256 and execute version probes; rerun create-new W3'
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          w3
forbid_1_pattern:       hardcode.*(?:/data/service/hnp|system).*(?:sign|objcopy)|copy.*(?:sign|objcopy).*shared
forbid_1_reason:        System paths are not guaranteed on every target and shared-directory writes violate task ownership.
forbid_1_consequence:   A package can compile but fail at package() or alter another task's environment.
forbid_2_pattern:       ignore.*(?:Error 127|signing.*missing)|skip.*sign
forbid_2_reason:        Unsigned OHOS ELF outputs are not valid runtime artifacts even when compilation passes.
forbid_2_consequence:   Target loading fails later with permission errors and masks the real package failure.
principles:             P007, P015, P020
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
